  "goodToKnow": "Der Faschismus is fascism, first under Mussolini in Italy from 1922. The Nazi regime is usually called Nationalsozialismus, though Faschismus is also used, especially in the former GDR, which called the Berlin Wall the antifaschistischer Schutzwall. The word comes from Italian fascio, a bundle of rods, a Roman symbol of power. Like all -ismus nouns, it's masculine."
